To me, the pc version 3.1.2 seems to suck.
I have the official devteam compilation that I got as a self-extracting
packet called NH312386.EXE, and I use a 486 with 8 MB ram.

1) I wasn't able to even start it from dos, it always gave the message
"CPU must be in real mode (not V86 mode) to run this program without VCPI.
(If you are using an EMS emulator, make sure that EMS isn't disabled)"
and returned me to the prompt. However, I got it running from windows.
OK, I replaced the NOEMS parameter with RAM where I start EMM386 in
my config.sys. Not happy, I've never needed EMS with any previous versions or
any other programs, they were happy enough with extended memory. And I
wouldn't like to emulate EMS instead of the programs using extended.
(OK, I know I can boot from a floppy whenever I want to play some nethack,
but I just wouldn't like to do it every time..)

2) The game doesn't seem to know how to use the BONES and LEVELS settings
in the .cnf file. I have the lines

HACKDIR=c:\games\nh312
LEVELS=c:\games\nh312\bones
SAVE=c:\games\nh312\bones;n

in my NETHACK.CNF, but it still wrote the levels and savefiles in the
HACKDIR instead of the bones directory. (Yes, I do have the directory
c:\games\nh312\bones, too.) Neither did the showexp option work although
the game said, when I checked with alt-v, that it can show exp points on
status line.
(OK, I might be able to live with these things, but I think they ARE bugs,
unless somebody says what I should have changed from the settings that
worked with the previous versions..)

3) Then I noticed that it was almost impossible to tell the rooms and
corridors from the background in bright daylight even when I turned the
brightness and contrast knobs on my old monitor to maximum, and I didn't
even find any low intensity codes in the termcap that could have caused
this and could be removed. Why is it the darkest possible gray that I
can't tell from black?
I can't play if I can't see a thing in my screen!

4) Just now, the game crashed.
I was picking up a potion of slime mold juice that I had named "slime".
The game crashed, and I got the message:
n . a potion called slime. Exception 117 (0x75) at EIP=71dc0
Call frame EIPs:
 0x00071dc0
 0x0007151f
 0x0003b14e
 0x00010e4c
 0x00001a32
 0x0004294b

5) I wasn't even able to recover the bloody crashed game after that!
I just got "Cannot exec go2.exe", when I tried to use the recover program.
Yes, the insurance option was set.


So, I'll just stick to the 3.1.1 until I get a better working 3.1.2.

